      <actel-cc:description>
When the CoreMP7 processor is instantiated in the design its interfaces to
the rest of the system (both inside and outside CoreConsole) are handled
through the CoreMP7Bridge.

The CoreMP7Bridge component has two functions. Firstly, it converts the native
signals from the CoreMP7 processor into an AMBA AHB master interface suitable
for connection to an AHB bus. Secondly, the CoreMP7Bridge includes circuitry which
deals with clock signals, reset signals and the signals which connect to the ARM
RealView ICE JTAG port.

      </actel-cc:description>
